"""
l2l3-audit - L2/L3 security assessment & attack tool for an isolated lab network.

Self-sufficient: run with `l2l3-audit <subcommand>` (uv bootstraps scapy on
first run). Needs root for raw sockets: `sudo l2l3-audit <subcommand> ...`.

Attack leg defaults to eth0 (-i). The watch leg is OPTIONAL (-w): scan
and full use it for traversal evidence when present, ghost needs it;
without it everything runs single-leg on the attack interface.

The tool never assumes a VLAN, and the port never gets the benefit of
the doubt: `scan` always auto-probes candidate VLANs (tagged and
untagged vantages alike - the switch may be misconfigured; use
--no-probe to stay passive). Leaks are enriched via `vlanenum`, VLANs
hijacked via `vlanhop` (or per-attack --tag).
"""

